  "name": "Question 3",
  "problem": "Find the two solutions to the equation $\\operatorname{cot}\u2061x=-\\sqrt{3}$ for ${0}^{\u2218}\\le x<{360}^{\u2218}.$\n\n**In ascending order,** the solutions are $x=$ \n{{field-1}}${}^{\u2218}$ and $x=$ \n{{field-2}}${}^{\u2218}.$",
  "worked_solution": "Recall that $\\operatorname{cot}\u2061x=\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{tan}\u2061x}.$ Therefore, the given equation is equivalent to\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{tan}\u2061x=-\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{3}}.\n$$\n\nNow, we find the principal value:\n\n$$\nx=\\operatorname{arctan}\u2061(-\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{3}})=-{30}^{\u2218}\n$$\n\nSince $-{30}^{\u2218}$ lies outside the given domain, it is not a solution.\n\nTo generate the solutions, we add integer multiples of ${180}^{\u2218}.$ Hence,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} & ={180}^{\u2218}+x={180}^{\u2218}-{30}^{\u2218}={150}^{\u2218}, \\\\ {x}_{2} & =2\\cdot {180}^{\u2218}+x=2\\cdot {180}^{\u2218}-{30}^{\u2218}={330}^{\u2218}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, in ascending order, the solutions are $x={150}^{\u2218}$ and $x={330}^{\u2218}.$",
